anized and not open to new ideas.\n\nGiven the criteria, crew cooperation and professional communication are important. B's issues may be severe. C's positive atmosphere suggests good crew cooperation, but difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric may be problematic. However, C's decision making is quick and correct, which is crucial. Also C's technical competence: understands complicated technology. So C might be a strong alternative.\n\nThus we could argue that while B has strong reliability and stress resilience, his communication issues could be a dealbreaker, and Candidate C offers better crew cooperation and decision quality, albeit with some concerns. So we might shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's point and bring in our own facts: C creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, understands complicated technology. Also note concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe can argue that C's strengths align well with decision quality and crew cooperation, which are critical, and his technical competence is solid. The concerns are less severe than B's nasty remarks? Possibly.\n\nThus we can propose Candidate C as provisional recommendation, explaining why.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\".\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: mention Agent 2's recommendation, acknowledge B's strengths, raise concerns about crew cooperation, bring up C's positive atmosphere and quick correct decisions, note concerns, but overall think C is better fit.\n\nProceed."}
